// A3 probe — the REAL silent failure: an `input` block with no `after` at all.
//
// Since globals in `stack.after` turn out to be a hard parse error (the other
// two probes), the ordering hazard is not an unresolved expression. It is a
// consumer whose `after` was simply forgotten. This fixture has a valid
// `input` pointing at the producer and NO ordering. Terramate accepts it,
// generates for it, and runs it in arbitrary order — no error, ever.
//
// That is risk R2, and it is why the G1 conftest policy has to exist.

stack {
  id   = "poc-no-after"
  name = "A3 probe — input with no after"
  tags = ["poc", "probe"]
}
